l (URU)\" -> \"Nacional\"\n s = re.sub(r\"\\([^)]*\\)\", \" \", s)\n # drop state suffix: \"Palmeiras-SP\" -> \"Palmeiras\", \"Barcelona-EQU\" -> \"Barcelona\"\n-s = re.sub(r\"-\\s*[A-Z]{2,3}\\s*$\", \"\", s.strip())\n+s = re.sub(r\"\\s*-\\s*[A-Z]{2,3}\\s*$\", \"\", s.strip())\n s = re.sub(r\"\\s+\", \" \", s).strip().lower()\n return s\n \n \n","additions":1,"deletions":1},"truncated":false},"title":"brazilian_soccer/loader.py","time":{"start":1788285696785,"end":1788285696787}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Wait — the regex must run BEFORE lowering? Currently: strip accents (removes accents, keeps case), drop parentheses, then suffix regex, then lower. \"Palmeiras-SP\" still uppercase at regex time. Good.\n\nBut note \"Barcelona-EQU\" in Libertadores... also matches like \"América - MG\" (Copa file uses \" - MG\" with spaces). suffix regex has `-\\s*`? Currently `r\"-\\s*[A-Z]{2,3}\\s*$\"` — \"América - MG\" has \" - MG\": dash before space. Pattern needs `\\s*-\\s*[A-Z]{2,3}$`. Update.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05e22391a001reqScWLBXJo3Fp","sessionID":"ses_fa1e38ef0ffeIEpkD87gUaZnL0","messageID":"msg_05e21e64f0019ukzvK33GuXFYB"}}
