{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788286126262,"sessionID":"ses_fa1e38ef0ffeIEpkD87gUaZnL0","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-95cb7773bcc010d5","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-tfe1ts5p/retort-af9123f1c3a8/brazilian_soccer/loader.py","newString":"    def head_to_head(self, team_a: str, team_b: str) -> list[Match]:\n        \"\"\"All matches where the two teams faced each other.\"\"\"\n        out = []\n        for m in self.matches:\n            a_home = name_matches(team_a, m.home)\n            a_away = name_matches(team_a, m.away)\n            b_home = name_matches(team_b, m.home)\n            b_away = name_matches(team_b, m.away)\n            if (a_home or b_home) and (a_away or b_away):\n                # both teams present, on opposite sides\n                if (a_home or a_away) and (b_home or b_away):\n                    out.append(m)\n        out.sort(key=lambda m: (m.date or datetime.min))\n        return out","oldString":"    def head_to_head(self, team_a: str, team_b: str) -> list[Match]:\n        out = []\n        for m in self.matches:\n            if name_matches(team_a, m.home) or name_matches(team_a, m.away):\n                if {name_matches(team_a, m.home), name_matches(team_a, m.away)} == {True, False}:\n                    if name_matches(team_b, m.home) or name_matches(team_b, m.away):\n                        out.append(m)\n        out.sort(key=lambda m: (m.date or datetime.min))\n        return out"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-tfe1ts5p/retort-af9123f1c3a8/brazilian_soccer/loader.py\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-tfe1ts5p/retort-af9123f1c3a8/brazilian_soccer/loader.py\n+++ /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-tfe1ts5p/retort-af9123f1c3a8/brazilian_soccer/loader.py\n@@ -442,14 +442,19 @@\n         if name_matches(team, m.home) or name_matches(team, m.away)\n     ]\n \n def head_to_head(self, team_a: str, team_b: str) -> list[Match]:\n+    \"\"\"All matches where the two teams faced each other.\"\"\"\n     out = []\n     for m in self.matches:\n-        if name_matches(team_a, m.home) or name_matches(team_a, m.away):\n-            if {name_matches(team_a, m.home), name_matches(team_a, m.away)} == {True, False}:\n-                if name_matches(team_b, m.home) or name_matches(team_b, m.away):\n-                    out.append(m)\n+        a_home = name_matches(team_a, m.home)\n+        a_away = name_matches(team_a, m.away)\n+        b_home = name_matches(team_b, m.home)\n+        b_away = name_matches(team_b, m.away)\n+        if (a_home or b_home) and (a_away or b_away):\n+            # both teams present, on opposite sides\n+            if (a_home or a_away) and (b_home or b_away):\n+                out.append(m)\n     out.sort(key=lambda m: (m.date or datetime.min))\n     return out\n \n def find_player(self, name: str) -> list[dict]:\n","filediff":{"file":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-tfe1ts5p/retort-af9123f1c3a8/brazilian_soccer/loader.py","patch":"Index: /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-tfe1ts5p/retort-af9123f1c3a8/brazilian_soccer/loader.py\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-tfe1ts5p/retort-af9123f1c3a8/brazilian_soccer/loader.py\n+++ /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-tfe1ts5p/retort-af9123f1c3a8/brazilian_soccer/loader.py\n@@ -442,14 +442,19 @@\n         if name_matches(team, m.home) or name_matches(team, m.away)\n     ]\n \n def head_to_head(self, team_a: str, team_b: str) -> list[Match]:\n+    \"\"\"All matches where the two teams faced each other.\"\"\"\n     out = []\n     for m in self.matches:\n-        if name_matches(team_a, m.home) or name_matches(team_a, m.away):\n-            if {name_matches(team_a, m.home), name_matches(team_a, m.away)} == {True, False}:\n-                if name_matches(team_b, m.home) or name_matches(team_b, m.away):\n-                    out.append(m)\n+        a_home = name_matches(team_a, m.home)\n+        a_away = name_matches(team_a, m.away)\n+        b_home = name_matches(team_b, m.home)\n+        b_away = name_matches(team_b, m.away)\n+        if (a_home or b_home) and (a_away or b_away):\n+            # both teams present, on opposite sides\n+            if (a_home or a_away) and (b_home or b_away):\n+                out.append(m)\n     out.sort(key=lambda m: (m.date or datetime.min))\n     return out\n \n def find_player(self, name: str) -> list[dict]:\n","additions":9,"deletions":4},"truncated":false},"title":"brazilian_soccer/loader.py","time":{"start":1788286126259,"end":1788286126261}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Wait — the head_to_head logic I wrote is convoluted and buggy (a match Flamengo vs Fluminense with query (Flamengo, Fluminense): first if true, set {T,F} ok, second if true → appended. But a match \"Fluminense vs Sao Paulo\": name_matches(flamengo, home)=F, away=F → first if fails → skip. Match \"Flamengo vs Flamengo\"? impossible. But query (Palmeiras, Santos), match \"Palmeiras vs Palmeiras\"? no. However match where team_a matches BOTH sides — impossible. Edge: match \"Santos-SP vs Santos-BA\"? unlikely. But cleaner:\n\n```python\ndef head_to_head(self, team_a, team_b):\n    out = []\n    for m in self.matches:\n        a_home = name_matches(team_a, m.home); a_away = name_matches(team_a, m.away)\n        b_home = name_matches(team_b, m.home); b_away = name_matches(team_b, m.away)\n        if (a_home or a_away) and (b_home or b_away):\n            # ensure they're on opposite sides (not same team matching both)\n            if (a_home or b_away) and (a_away or b_home):  # hmm\n```\nSimple correct: match qualifies if one of {home,away} matches a exclusively and other matches b. Given a != b teams: condition: (a_home and b_away) or (a_away and b_home) or (b_home and a_away) ... that's the same two cases. But also a_home and b_home both true (both match same team) — degenerate. Use:\n\nqualifies = (a_home or a_away) and (b_home or b_away) and not (a_home and a_away) and not (b_home and b_away) — plus not both matching same side... Simplest: qualifies = (a_home and b_away) or (a_away and b_home) or (a_home and b_home is wrong)...\n\nFor team_a==team_b query degenerate. I'll use: `((a_home or b_home) and (a_away or b_away))` — i.e., one query matches home side and other matches away side, in some assignment:\nqualifies = (a_home or b_home) and (a_away or b_away) and team sides are distinct — since home != away always in real data, and a/b distinct queries... For \"Flamengo vs Fluminense\" and match \"Fluminense vs Flamengo\": a_away? a=flamengo matches away → True; b_home=fluminense matches home → True → qualifies. Match \"Flamengo vs Vasco\": a_home=T; a_away=F; b_away=F → (a_away or b_away)=F → no. Good. Match \"Fluminense vs Vasco\": (a_home or b_home): a_home=F, b_home=T → T; (a_away or b_away)=F → no. Good.\n\nRewrite head_to_head with that.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05e28c1ba001fMXapYpB36sJcz","sessionID":"ses_fa1e38ef0ffeIEpkD87gUaZnL0","messageID":"msg_05e288468001ycM4QmTDqFyCsR"}}
