{"type":"text","timestamp":1788286341311,"sessionID":"ses_fa1e38ef0ffeIEpkD87gUaZnL0","part":{"id":"prt_05e2c019d00155rcS7UZOOscNt","messageID":"msg_05e2bf7ba001S939DEhbyyT60l","sessionID":"ses_fa1e38ef0ffeIEpkD87gUaZnL0","type":"text","text":"Done. The Brazilian Soccer MCP server is implemented and verified end-to-end.\n\n**Files created:**\n- `server.py` — MCP server (FastMCP, stdio transport) with 14 tools: match/team/player/competition queries, head-to-head, standings, champion, stats, biggest wins, best records\n- `brazilian_soccer/loader.py` — loads all 6 CSVs into normalized `Match` records; handles ISO/Brazilian date formats, UTF-8 accents, and two-tier team-name matching (a plain query like \"Palmeiras\" matches `Palmeiras-SP`, but `Atlético-MG` never merges with `Atlético-PR`)\n- `brazilian_soccer/queries.py` — stats, standings (3 pts/win), h2h, player search, formatting\n- `tests/test_bdd.py` — 39 BDD-style tests mirroring the TASK.md Gherkin scenarios\n- `requirements.txt` (`mcp>=1.2.0,<2` — mcp 2.x renamed FastMCP, so it's pinned)\n\n**Key data problems solved along the way:**\n- Three files overlap on the same seasons (e.g. 2019 Brasileirão in 3 files) — `competition_matches()` picks the single best source per season to avoid double-counting\n- \"Serie A\" in the BR dataset is aliased to \"Brasileirão\"; state-suffix stripping was made query-aware to keep same-name teams from different states distinct\n\n**Verified:** all 39 tests pass in ~4s; live tool calls produce correct results (2019 champion: Flamengo, 90 pts, 28W/6D/4L; Neymar top-rated Brazilian at 92; Fla-Flu h2h correct across 2003–2023); performance tests assert <2s lookups and <5s aggregates; stdio handshake lists all 14 tools.","time":{"start":1788286337437,"end":1788286341305}}}
